     "explanation": "C = Q / V = 0.02 coulombs / 10 volts = 0.002 farads, which equals 2000 microfarads. Capacitance is charge stored per volt: this device packs 0.002 coulombs onto its plates for every volt applied. A larger C would mean even more charge crammed on per volt. Note the farad is a large unit — real capacitors are usually rated in microfarads (µF) or picofarads (pF).",
