    {
     "type": "application",
     "title": "Putting It All Together",
     "content": "Let's gather everything into a single, sturdy mental picture you'll keep for life.\n\n**What light IS.** An electromagnetic wave is an oscillating **electric field** and **magnetic field**, locked in step and perpendicular to each other and to the direction of travel — a **transverse** wave. Each changing field regenerates the other, so the wave is **self-propagating** and needs **no medium**. That's why sunlight crosses empty space.\n\n**The one speed.** In vacuum, every EM wave travels at **c ≈ 3 × 10⁸ m/s** — radio, light, and gamma alike.\n\n**The one equation.** **c = f × λ.** Since c is fixed, **frequency and wavelength trade off**: higher frequency means shorter wavelength. And via **E = h × f**, higher frequency also means **more energy per photon** — which is why radio is harmless and gamma is lethal.\n\n**The one spectrum.** A single continuous ribbon ordered by frequency: **radio → microwaves → infrared → visible → ultraviolet → X-rays → gamma.** Visible light — red at 700 nm to violet at 400 nm — is the thin slice your eyes evolved to catch, because it's where the Sun shines brightest and the atmosphere is clear.\n\n**Try it yourself:**\n• Feel your own **infrared** — cup your hands near your cheeks and sense the warmth radiating off them.\n• Point a phone **camera** at a TV remote and press a button; many cameras see the **infrared** flash your eyes can't.\n• Next time you microwave food, remember: you're bathing it in the same phenomenon as starlight, just at a frequency tuned to spin water molecules.\n\nOne wave. Seven names. The whole of light.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial\">Putting It All Together</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"23\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial\">The whole of light in one picture</text><rect x=\"120\" y=\"150\" width=\"860\" height=\"150\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.10)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#6366f1\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial\">WHAT IT IS</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"245\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial\">transverse wave: E &#8869; B &#8869; travel</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"283\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial\">self-propagating, needs no medium</text><rect x=\"120\" y=\"320\" width=\"420\" height=\"150\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.10)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"370\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#10b981\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial\">ONE SPEED</text><text x=\"330\" y=\"415\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial\">c &#8776; 3 &#215; 10&#8312; m/s</text><text x=\"330\" y=\"450\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial\">all bands, in vacuum</text><rect x=\"560\" y=\"320\" width=\"420\" height=\"150\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.10)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"770\" y=\"370\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial\">TWO EQUATIONS</text><text x=\"770\" y=\"415\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial\">c = f &#215; &#955;</text><text x=\"770\" y=\"450\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial\">E = h &#215; f</text><rect x=\"120\" y=\"490\" width=\"860\" height=\"230\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.08)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"535\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial\">ONE SPECTRUM (low f &#8594; high f)</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"580\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial\">radio &#8594; micro &#8594; infrared &#8594;</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"620\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#10b981\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial\">VISIBLE (700nm red &#8211; 400nm violet) &#8594;</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"660\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#ec4899\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial\">UV &#8594; X-rays &#8594; gamma</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"700\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial\">higher f = shorter &#955; = more energy</text><rect x=\"120\" y=\"740\" width=\"860\" height=\"200\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.08)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"790\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial\">Try it yourself</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"835\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial\">feel the infrared warmth off your hands</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"875\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial\">watch a remote's IR flash in a phone camera</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"918\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#10b981\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Arial\">One wave. Seven names. All of light.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "The complete picture: what light is, its one speed, its two equations, and its one continuous spectrum."
     }
    }
