     "type": "concept",
     "title": "The Quiet Wonder of Unification",
     "content": "Take a breath and appreciate what actually happened in the history you just retraced.\n\nFor most of human time, **electricity** (sparks, shocks, lightning) and **magnetism** (lodestones, compasses) looked like two unrelated curiosities. Nobody suspected a link. Then, in a single century, a handful of people — **Oersted, Ampere, Faraday, Maxwell, Einstein** — showed they were one thing. Two mysteries collapsed into one law.\n\nThis is the pattern physics keeps repeating, and it is the deepest reason to care:\n• Newton unified the **falling apple** and the **orbiting Moon** into one gravity.\n• Maxwell unified **electricity, magnetism, and light**.\n• Later physicists unified **electromagnetism with the weak nuclear force** into the **electroweak** force — a real, established result honored with a Nobel Prize.\n\nEach step, the universe gets **simpler**, not more complicated. Fewer laws explain more things. Many physicists suspect all four forces of nature may ultimately be one — that search for a final unification is still open, at the frontier, unfinished. **(That final theory is advanced and not yet confirmed.)**\n\nYou now stand inside that grand tradition. When you flip a switch or feel sunlight, you are watching a unification that took humanity thousands of years to see — and that you can now explain.",
