     "explanation": "The through-line of the whole book is unification. Electric and magnetic effects are not two separate forces that merely cooperate; they are one electromagnetic force seen from different frames of motion, which special relativity makes precise, and which quantum electrodynamics describes as photon exchange. Saying they are separate, or that one is merely a side effect of the other, misses the central insight. From charge and Coulomb's law all the way to relativity and QED, it is one force wearing different masks.",
